rows=[(548, 'small-care', 'Small care', 'The blessing compares a child growing with little care to roadside grass flowers nourished by water from a leaking vessel. Suggest the modest life that flourishes, without inventing a mother-child portrait or turning care into a decorative abundance.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 delicate watercolor and sparse graphite, a low close view of a small irregular patch of roadside grass with three or four tiny pale wildflowers growing in damp earth. At the extreme upper left a cropped ordinary terracotta water vessel has a small worn pinhole near its lower wall, letting a thin damp trace descend to the earth; one drop, not a fountain. The vessel is upright and supported on soil, not precarious or broken into pieces. Roots are hidden, leaves overlap and some flower heads turn away. Most of the right half is soft pale warm earth with a few indistinct grass marks. Modest indirect morning light, tender everyday resilience. No elaborate garden, overlarge blooms, people, religious emblems, butterflies, idealised family, text or staged clutter. Keep water and gravity causal, selectively observe a flower and damp patch, let other edges dissolve into opaque ivory paper.'), (550, 'an-unwound-afternoon', 'An unwound afternoon', 'After intimacy and ageing, the poem’s afternoon has forgotten to wind the wall clock. The still clock is a restrained anchor for time and absence, without literalising the erotic memory or the final metaphysical bird-cage image.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 matte gouache and graphite study of a modest old mechanical wall clock on a plain warm grey domestic wall, slightly off-centre left at an ordinary upward viewing angle. A simple oval dark wood case, round cream dial with twelve short unnumbered tick marks and exactly two slender hands meeting at one central spindle; no numerals, brand or writing. A narrow lower glass panel reveals a single plain brass pendulum hanging straight down at rest. Case joins, wall mounting, dial perspective and glass reflection physically plausible, nothing ornate. Soft indirect afternoon light across the right half of the bare wall, enough to feel lived-in but no added furniture, flowers, photographs, dust spectacle, cracked plaster or dramatic sunbeam. Unequal quiet paint edges and restrained graphite structure. A memory’s silence rather than antique-shop glamour or surreal melting clock.'), (551, 'river-and-rice', 'River and rice', 'Amid the poem’s many Odisha places, crafts and foods, the river’s maternal presence and surrounding paddy offer one coherent landscape. Keep it an imagined literary view, not an invented panorama or an assembly of monuments.', 'Original horizontal 3:2 broad matte gouache and a few soft charcoal strokes, an imagined Odisha agricultural landscape seen from a modest raised earthen bank. Quiet green paddy fields occupy the lower left, their uneven bunds meeting a broad river bending gently toward the right distance. Sparse rice stalks only near the foreground edge; middle fields merge into subdued green planes. A low far bank and faint blue-grey hills under ordinary hazy daylight, generous pale sky in the upper third. Believable water level, river banks and field drainage, no impossibly floating plots. Human cultivated scale without people as decorative marks. No temple, famous monument, deity, maps, flag, boat, bird, craft motifs, food collage, lettering or tourist sunset. Warm earth, varied paddy green, muted river grey and distant blue. Preserve expansive ordinary fertility and care with selective detail; do not render every stalk or cloud.')]
items=[]
